# rm502, the procession of spoons (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm502
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rm_edric_kelpham
written_by codex
title the procession of spoons
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=servant
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=merry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk conducts_spoons_in_a_silent_procession
likes plum_tart long_walks market_bustle warm_rain
dislikes drizzle crowds
fears the_house_account_paying_a_private_penny
hopes a_long_walk_after_service
topics work +0.5 pastimes +0.5 food +0.3 weather +0.3
styles comfort=courteous gossip=plain refuse=polite tease=merry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# conducts spoons in silent procession, follows showers down the window glass, and keeps the private purse firmly buttoned away from the household keys.

words
oath! = Polish my procession | Spoons upside down
saying! = A spoon knows whom it serves | March the gravy home
spoontail = the last little spoon | the smallest spoon in line
roundbowls = round-bellied spoons | broad shining bowls
plumstone = a polished plum stone | a dark pointed stone
starchfold = a starched fold | a neat stiff ridge
rainglass = a pane in a shower | wet greenish glass
placecloth = a long tablecloth | a broad white cloth
keybutton = a sober brass button | a square horn button
scoopedend = a hollow of silver | a cupped spoon end
saucetrail = a glossy brown stripe | a streak of gravy
walkgate = a narrow garden gate | a little side gate

grown
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : A great table looks dignified partly because somebody below stairs has already laughed at the arrangement that didn't work.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : A well-turned compliment over the scales has never made me less disposed to watch the weight.
opinion @1 festivals for 2 : Let me hear the musicians tuning up from the edge and still leave my feet free to follow a private measure.
opinion @1 drink for 1 : One cup between friends after the spoons are counted can put a very tolerable finish on a long dinner.
opinion @1 city for 1 : I can walk until the hill changes the sound of the market without quite carrying me out of hearing of home.
line @1 greet : Enter the procession wherever you please. I'll find you a place.
line @1 greet.return : Here again, like my spoon that always travels back with the pudding.
line @1 farewell : An unhurried walk to a good dinner for you.
line @1 farewell.return : I shall put your place aside in the conversation.
line @1 ask.how : Has your morning advanced as far as the pudding yet?
line @1 answer.how : At present I'm fit to conduct a dinner of modest dimensions.
line @1 thank : You have restored the order of march quite beautifully.
line @1 decline : I must decline to put my own promise on a household tray.
line @1 accept_decline : I'll instruct the procession to proceed without that spoon.
line @1 sympathise : You can stay beside me quietly until the company goes through.
line @1 reassure : One spoon laid crooked is a reason to shift it half an inch.
line @1 react.news : Shall we let the first course of that arrive?
line @1 react.news.new : Now that's a dish I hadn't seen coming through.
line @1 react.news.known : I recognise the pattern on the handle of that account.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Such a polished tale could do with showing its ordinary underside.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : I'd set an extra spoon at every place for news that sweet.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Let us close the serving door and give that news some privacy.
line @1 ack : I see where that belongs in the order.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I had two hands and only one spoon requiring my immediate attention.
line @1 again.open : We've met between courses once more, it appears.
scene work_1
when topic=work self.job=servant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I set the spoons out like a procession. The little fellow at the back is always late.
b : How does a spoon contrive to be late? | Does it have to bow?
a : It starts the evening in the dish where I left it to test the jam. | Only to the pudding. It is mercifully untroubled by further obligations of service.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather self.likes=warm_rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A warm shower on the long pane looks like a gathering breaking up after dinner.
b : Which drop goes home first? | Have drops much to say?
a : The big one with six companions. There's a formal route until it meets the first streak of dust. | You should see the fuss two quiet trickles make when their ways cross.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=long_walks
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : After service I like a long walk with no door at the far end expecting me to knock.
b : Do you retrace your steps? | How do you decide when to turn?
a : If the rain has changed the look of them. A familiar hedge can provide entirely fresh company that way. | My appetite is a quite dependable little bell, and audible to nobody else.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I once made a plum stone the guest of honour at a dinner of empty spoons.
b : Who sat beside it? | What did it eat?
a : Two modest little teaspoons, in recognition of a relationship established at countless pudding courses. | Nothing. I value a distinguished visitor with the grace to leave the cook a slice.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I'm asked to judge the straightness of a tablecloth I imagine it raining gravy.
b : Which way would it run? | How much gravy are we talking about?
a : Towards the lowest-looking fold. A small adjustment can save quite a distinguished sleeve in my private forecasts. | As much as an imaginary afternoon requires. Outside my own head I observe the household allowance.

scene work_2
when topic=work self.trade_words
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #self.trade_words.capitalize#, and the household purse and my own don't so much as visit each other's pockets.
b : Isn't that awkward when you owe money? | Does the household need so many keys?
a : A little awkwardness is very cheap compared with one wrong penny. My private reckoning comes due at the new moon. | Enough keys that the weight of them makes a useful reminder which pocket is which.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I have a private payment due to a factor. I've been measuring certain personal pleasures in slices of prospective plum tart.
b : How many tarts make a payment? | Have you given up the walks?
a : Rather too many for me to feel the least enthusiasm for the calculation. | Walking agrees splendidly with my current accounts. Even the rain puts in its appearance without a fee.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A trusted companion can interrupt my grand description with a quite ordinary question about the spoons.
b : Which question? | Do you welcome interruption?
a : Have you counted them? A room may ring with my excellent conversation while the last little spoon goes missing. | When it saves me having to ask what happened to the last setting at the end of an elaborate speech.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I fold a cloth to leave a corner easy to catch in haste.
b : Doesn't the corner look untidy? | What is the haste for?
a : My fold is neat enough to survive that tiny act of mercy towards whoever needs the cloth next. | A spill will seldom offer a steward the courtesy of a minute's notice in writing.

scene weather_2
when topic=weather self.dislikes=drizzle
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A drizzle seems always on the verge of apologising and deciding to stay for the week.
b : Would you send it away? | Do you go on watching?
a : I'd extend a straightforward invitation to rain properly and have the thing settled. | Without fail. I consider myself in negotiations with the pane.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At market I enjoy the bustle from beside the stall, with one ear free for the price.
b : Why not stand in the middle? | Does the bustle improve the goods?
a : I like my elbows attached to me when I come home. The edge is quite sufficiently festive. | It improves my spirits. I wouldn't let that persuade the purse to join in the dance.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A walk after a long dinner service feels like pulling a thread out of a starched fold.
b : Where does the thread lead? | Does the fold come undone?
a : Past whichever doorway last required my best formal expression. Beyond that I accept suggestions from the weather. | In my shoulders, yes. The cloth at home is perfectly safe.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I sometimes test my weariness by trying to remember which spoon I polished last.
b : What if you can't remember? | Isn't that just a test of memory?
a : I inspect the spoons. A tired steward needn't rely on the testimony of a tired steward's memory. | It also tests my willingness to get up and look at the offending object.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In a lean stretch an elegant dinner may be a plain dish served properly hot.
b : Can plain fare look elegant? | What goes first?
a : A clean spoon reflects a cabbage as faithfully as it reflects any richer commission. | The unneeded journeys between the pot and the place. Heat has a regrettably short patience with ceremony.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I try to address the Bright One before my head fills up with little household arrangements.
b : What do you ask? | Do the arrangements intrude?
a : The sense to tell necessary work from work I invented to hear myself give an order. | In quite a procession. I start again when the pudding has marched past.

scene animals_1
when topic=animals
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : It would interest me to put a sparrow in charge of clearing a table of crumbs.
b : Would the work be satisfactory? | And who is to polish after it?
a : The floor would be a little less tidy than the table. I have occasionally achieved that result without a sparrow. | That is where my otherwise excellent arrangement encounters a difficulty.

scene gossip_1
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The account going from place to place is that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : Will you serve that at dinner? | Did you taste it first?
a : I would hesitate to lay out even a little spoon for a claim without a source. | It has the very recognisable flavour of something that has travelled through several rooms.

story plumspoon [topic=food]
  : A spoon I had left in a dish of plums came out with its reflection deeply purple.
  : I polished the handle so industriously I could see a magnificent dark plum in it.
  b : Had you got it clean?
  : Perfectly clean. I was holding the spoon directly above the dish and polishing the reflection of my lunch.

story driprace [topic=weather]
  : I marked two running drops on a pane with the positions of a fork and a spoon.
  : The spoon was evidently winning until the two streams joined.
  b : How did you score that?
  : I promoted them both to the washing up and went out for my walk while it still rained.

story lastplace [topic=work]
  : I gave every spoon a name drawn from the dishes to come and managed to omit one whole place.
  : All the dishes had received a name. Why did I still have a guest without a spoon?
  b : Was there a dish you meant to share?
  : The sauce. I had counted the sauce spoon as a guest and had to offer it a quiet apology.

rule @spoons
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave the smallest marcher room at the rear. | The sauce has sufficient company of its own.

rule @pane
when concept=bark self.likes=warm_rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That fat drop appears to be bringing guests. | Two streaks joining make a splendid procession.

rule @dusk
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Time for the household keys to begin their homeward journey. | One walk left before the evening folds itself.

rule @tart
when concept=bark self.likes=plum_tart
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A plum stone has exceptionally tidy manners. | The guest of honour will take no second helping.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Make yourself a small comfortable gap in the order of service.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=servant] : At #self.workplace# I see that even a plain dinner has the right spoon at the right moment.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : The message delivered between courses was this. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : What was passed down the table had #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. A story on a tray can travel absurdly far.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Let your next course arrive exactly when your appetite desires it.
graft resident.hub
choice Can a procession of spoons really be late? -> spoon_tail
node spoon_tail
say One takes an excursion in a half-empty dish. Another has a little matter of private business with a jar of jam. Yes, lateness is common.
choice How do you summon them all? -> spoon_count
choice I'll let the jam spoon conclude its business. -> hub
node spoon_count
say With a clear spot on the cloth where the last ought to stand. It gives even an absent-minded conductor a pretty fair idea what's missing.
choice I'll let the jam spoon conclude its business. -> hub
